--TEST--
Core\Crypto::agree agrees over the two curves of the roster and refuses every other pairing of kinds — a kind that agrees nothing, or two keys on different curves — each with the one LogicError sentence, counted over the whole matrix — `rule:core-classes/crypto-interop-tier`, `rule:core-api/shape-rules`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Agreement over a sweep: every kind of `Core\Crypto\KeyKind` is offered to
// every other, and each cell either agrees or is the one refusal. Asked one
// cell at a time this looks right for whichever pairing a member happened to
// implement; asked as a matrix, a member that had let an Ed25519 pair reach a
// curve, or let two curves be crossed, fails here. The three drawn kinds are
// drawn, since what a pair holds does not change which cells agree, and the RSA
// rows are one issued file read under both schemes.
string $rsaPkcs8 = "";

array<Core\Crypto\KeyKind> $kinds = [
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::P256,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::X25519,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::Ed25519,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::RsaPkcs1,
    Core\Crypto\KeyKind::RsaPss,
];

array<Core\Crypto\KeyPair> $pairs = [];
array<Core\Crypto\PublicKey> $publics = [];
foreach (Core\Arr::range(0, 4) as int $kind) {
    Core\Crypto\KeyPair $held = $kind < 3
        ? Core\Crypto::generateKeyPair($kinds[$kind])
        : Core\Crypto\KeyPair::read(Core\Encoding::fromHex($rsaPkcs8), $kinds[$kind]);
    $pairs = Core\Arr::append($pairs, $held);
    $publics = Core\Arr::append($publics, $held->publicKey());
}

// The two cells that agree are the two curves with themselves. Every other one
// of the twenty-five is the same `LogicError`: both keys are the program's own,
// so there is nobody a verdict could be about.
int $cells = 0;
int $secrets = 0;
array<string> $said = [];
foreach (Core\Arr::range(0, 4) as int $mine) {
    foreach (Core\Arr::range(0, 4) as int $theirs) {
        $cells += 1;
        try {
            secret bytes $shared = Core\Crypto::agree($pairs[$mine], $publics[$theirs]);
            if ($mine == $theirs && $mine < 2) {
                $secrets += 1;
            } else {
                echo "row ", $mine, " agreed with column ", $theirs, "\n";
            }
        } catch (LogicError $notAPair) {
            $said = Core\Arr::append($said, $notAPair->message);
        }
    }
}
echo "cells ", $cells, "\n";
echo "agreed ", $secrets, " of 2", "\n";
echo "refused ", Core\Arr::count($said), " of ", $cells - 2, "\n";

int $oneSentence = 0;
foreach ($said as string $message) {
    if ($message == $said[0]) {
        $oneSentence += 1;
    }
}
echo "one sentence ", $oneSentence, " of ", Core\Arr::count($said), "\n";
echo $said[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--
cells 25
agreed 2 of 2
refused 23 of 23
one sentence 23 of 23
Core\Crypto::agree(): these two keys are not two ends of one agreement. Both have to be of one curve, `P256` or `X25519` — `Ed25519` signs and agrees nothing, and neither RSA kind agrees at all.
